        "original_id": "b659ce6a-f37f-53c8-aeb8-d755c19192bb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ann M. O'Leary, Hillary Rodham Clinton, Bill Clinton\n- Roles: political advisor, lawyer, nonprofit leader, United States Senator, United States Secretary of State\n- Organizations: Bill Clinton administration, United States Senate, Obama Administration\n- Topics: early childhood education, Hillary Clinton's Senate career, presidential campaigns\n\nFacts:\n- Hillary Rodham Clinton served as a United States Senator from New York from January 3, 2001, to January 21, 2009.\n- Ann M. O'Leary is an American political advisor, lawyer, and nonprofit leader who specializes in early childhood education.\n- Ann M. O'Leary worked in the Bill Clinton administration and for Hillary Rodham Clinton during Clinton's time as First Lady, Senate career, and 2008 and 2016 presidential campaigns.\n- Hillary Rodham Clinton resigned from the United States Senate on January 21, 2009, to become United States Secretary of State in the Obama Administration.",
